# ReconForge CLI — Modular Pentest Recon Pipeline

A CLI-based reconnaissance toolkit for **authorized security testing**.

> ⚠️ Authorized use only. Run this tool only on systems you own or where you have explicit written permission.

## Current status

This repository now contains a working Python CLI with the following commands:

- `subdomains`: generates a built-in common subdomain list and resolves DNS
- `alive`: probes resolved hosts for HTTP/HTTPS reachability
- `ports`: scans a small top-port set
- `report`: writes a Markdown + JSON summary
- `run`: executes `subdomains -> alive -> ports -> report`

## Install

```bash
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -e .
```

## Usage

```bash
reconforge run --domain example.com --out runs/example.com
```

Or modular:

```bash
reconforge subdomains --domain example.com --out runs/example.com
reconforge alive --input runs/example.com/subdomains/resolved.txt --out runs/example.com
reconforge ports --input runs/example.com/alive/alive.txt --out runs/example.com
reconforge report --input runs/example.com
```

## Output structure

```text
runs/example.com/
├── scope/
├── subdomains/
│   ├── all.txt
│   ├── resolved.txt
│   ├── failed.txt
│   └── sources.json
├── alive/
│   ├── alive.txt
│   └── alive.json
├── ports/
│   ├── services.txt
│   └── ports.json
├── web/
│   └── titles.txt
├── report/
│   ├── report.md
│   └── summary.json
└── logs/
```
